              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Sanskrit for an island, then the Sanskrit for a shore."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: विद्यालयः",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "विद्यालयः (vidyālayaḥ) — \"a school\": विद्या, \"knowledge\", with आलयः, \"home\". A school is a home of knowledge."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Vidyālaya is built from vidyā, \"knowledge\", from the root √vid, and ālaya, \"a dwelling\". MW records it as \"seat of learning, a school\" only from a nineteenth-century dictionary, so the everyday school sense is recent."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Knowledge plus home."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
