          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Adhyāpaka is built on the causative of adhi + the root √i, \"to go over, study\": \"one who makes others study\" (MW, CDIAL 278). Worn down, it became jhā, the name of a Maithili Brahman community."
            }
          ]
        },
